From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 07:59:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): give a busy-chat send that could not be queued
 back to the composer (#770)

* fix(desktop): give a busy-chat send that could not be queued back to the composer

A send the owner admitted whose turn was then refused because another writer
held the chat's turn lease (serve turn refused at once, gateway lease-wait
timeout, taken-over chat; failure_reason session_busy) lost the user's words:
Enter had already cleared the composer.

- tui_gateway: message.complete forwards failure_reason=session_busy.
- Desktop: the live frame and the failed_turn hydration row mark the refusal
  (ChatMessage.refusedSend); the composer offers the refused words back once,
  after anything typed meanwhile, as a new message (fresh submission id).
- Nothing runs twice: one offer per scope+text (survives reload, released by a
  newer user turn); Retry/Take over withdraws an untouched offer.
- SESSION_OWNER_BUSY (refused before admission) already keeps the draft; now
  covered by tests.

Follow-up of #765.

* refactor(tui_gateway): move message.complete outcome flags into _structured_outcome_fields

Keeps _complete_turn_payload under the code-health CC target after the
session_busy failure_reason was added.
